=== attack audit — v5 vs heuristic on W0Base
  100 episodes, win_rate 0.810, 22.5 turns/ep

  attack rate                 1081/1605   0.674 [0.650,0.696]   creatures sent / could have attacked
    reference would send       641/1605   0.399 [0.376,0.424]   same denominator: the size of any over/under shoot
    reference (CA) would send   555/1605   0.346 [0.323,0.369]
  attack-optimality            510/786    0.649 [0.615,0.681]   UPPER BOUND: includes no-choice combats
    ...where a choice existed   510/786    0.649 [0.615,0.681]   the honest one
  attack-optimality (CA)       541/786    0.688 [0.655,0.720]   reference charges for the crack-back

  score gap (myopic)         1818 over 786 combats
  score gap (CA)             1775
  missed lethal              1   (own category, never a gap)
  errors UNDER / OVER        63 / 208   (sent fewer / more than ref)
  truncated subsets/replies  0 / 0
  combats with no choice     0   (MATCH there is the position's)

  cost: policy search 317 ms total, 0.40 ms/combat; audit 317 ms (instrument, not play)
  nodes: 933k resolve() calls, 1187 per combat

  READ WITH: the reference is one combat deep and prices at zero
  the fact that an attacker cannot block next turn, so it
  over-credits attacking. A rise in attack-optimality alongside
  a rise in attack rate is partly tautological; the CA row and
  the UNDER/OVER split are what separate them.
